{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Visits Vanessa at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Graveyard Shift "}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A phrasal verb is a phrase formed with a verb + preposition. <br/><br/>The combination of the verb and preposition changes the meaning of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are some phrasal verbs related to work:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "to follow up -- to return to a subject already discussed<br/>to run into -- to encounter, to experience<br/>to set up -- to establish, to plan<br/>to turn out -- to end by being a certain way<br/>to fill (you) in -- to inform, to tell (you)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You conjugate phrasal verbs in the same way you conjugate other verbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Question Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I go out on Saturdays.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you go out on Saturdays?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am going out this evening.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Are you going out this evening?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I went out last Saturday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Did you go out last Saturday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have gone out every Saturday this month.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have you gone out every Saturday this month?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect tense\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I want to follow up on our meeting last week. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sometimes we run into problems when we are short staffed."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Discussing How to Deal with Problems "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "One way to discuss how to deal with problems is to say what you would do if you were in someone else's situation. This is a polite way of communicating if you use the modals <span class=\"italic\">would</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could</span>.<br/><br/><span class=\"italic\">I would ... <br/>I wouldn't ... <br/>You Could ... </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are examples of Vanessa and Bruce suggesting how to deal with the problems in the restaurant. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bruce</span>:  Sometimes we run into problems when we are short staffed.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  I wouldn't worry about it. We planned the work schedule already.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: We have three servers, two bus people, a kitchen manager, a soup and sauce cook and a ma\u00eetre d'. Isn't that enough?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Bruce</span>: You could add an extra sous chef and maybe a bartender. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to make sure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to verify"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to make sure we have enough staff. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about working in a restaurant."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fill in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to inform"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll fill you in tomorrow about my decision."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "graveyard shift"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "work hours during the late evening or night"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The graveyard shift is  from 10:00 p.m. to 4:00 a.m. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "server"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "waiter or waitress; a person who waits on tables in a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have three servers working tonight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bus person"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "person who prepares and cleans up tables in a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Two bus people are also on staff this evening. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ma\u00eetre d'"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the host or hostess; the person who escorts customers to their place in a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To become a ma\u00eetre d', you should start as a server."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le07ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, choose a type of restaurant. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your friend doesn't know what to order.  Think of different items that would be on the menu."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Start your dialogue talking about the menu choices."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the options."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about what is advisable. Use <span class=\"italic\">\u201cought to\u201d</span> at least one time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Conclude your dialogue with a decision for each person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a total of 10 lines."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about food items on a menu."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about different options."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say what is advisable."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about jobs and work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss how to deal with problems."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what is advisable."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What types of jobs do people do in restaurants?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Would you like to work in a restaurant? Why or why not?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Whe